---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SupportState from '../components/SupportState.astro';
import { PROJECT } from '../content/wording';
---
<BaseLayout title="Bridging the Laptop-to-Cluster Gap" description="Public BSSw Fellowship guidance for translating multi-service laptop workflows to scheduler-managed HPC systems." canonicalPath="/">
<h1>Bridging the Laptop-to-Cluster Gap</h1>
<p class="lede">A public, static guide for translating multi-service laptop workflows into scheduler-managed, rootless-container workflows on shared HPC systems.</p>
<section><h2>Who this is for</h2><p>Scientific software practitioners, first-time HPC learners, workflow maintainers, research computing staff, educators, and fellowship reviewers. All published content is anonymous-access: <strong>No account is required</strong>.</p></section>
<section><h2>Current release</h2><p><strong>{PROJECT.release}</strong>. The two Milestone 1 modules and supporting guidance are published; Module 2 clearly labels representative-environment execution as unvalidated until evidence is added.</p><p><a href="/releases/v0-1-0/">Read release status</a> or <a href="/milestones/1/">review every Milestone 1 deliverable</a>.</p></section>
<section><h2>Get started</h2><div class="cards"><article class="card"><h3>Understand the model</h3><p><a href="/guide/scheduler-as-orchestrator/">Scheduler as Orchestrator</a> maps Compose responsibilities to HPC.</p></article><article class="card"><h3>Prepare safely</h3><p><a href="/start/">Check prerequisites and local adaptations</a> before any execution step.</p></article><article class="card"><h3>Try the baseline</h3><p><a href="/guide/baseline-single-node-pattern/">Run the bounded service-plus-workers pattern</a> and verify results.</p></article></div></section>
<section><h2>Find and reuse</h2><p>Browse the complete <a href="/resources/">resource index</a>, durable <a href="/diagnostics/">diagnostic registry</a>, or public <a href={PROJECT.repository}>Companion repository</a>.</p></section>
<SupportState />
</BaseLayout>
